--- final message ---
The strategy is ready (`status: ready`), and I wrote `paper_strategy.json` and `paper_strategy.md`. The JSON parses; I did not run the paper validator, as instructed.

**Framing.** The paper is thesis-first: a selection-aware reporter for the score of a configuration picked after prompt search. The reporter is an empirical-Bayes hierarchical latent-difficulty model that gives a 90% posterior interval from the search log alone. The final evaluation completed with outcome `qualified`. Its interval score is 0.1449, against 0.2202 for the naive Wilson reporter, 0.1974 for Bonferroni and 0.2461 for question resampling. Coverage is 0.929.

**Conditional claims.** Per-case numbers from the final episodes show a mixed picture, so the plan foregrounds the following and the claims stay conditional on those settings:
- **Real halving and large N:** the method is roughly on par with naive on real successive-halving (P4) and on large-N (P6), with coverage below 0.90 there.
- **Resampling reporter:** it is slightly better on several real exhaustive cases but very poor under halving.
- **Scope:** one 0.5B model, MMLU-Pro, 24 prompt configurations, two searchers.
- **Per-case caveat:** the per-case numbers come from episode records whose diagnostics are marked unverified; the writer is told to recompute them and to treat the aggregate metrics as authoritative.

**Scope of the evidence.**
- There is no `downstream_study` block, so the plan makes no downstream claims.
- Three attempts were scored, none unscored. Only the frozen winner has a final evaluation, so the two other variants appear only as a search-stage width-versus-coverage comparison.
- The cached model outcomes were shipped with the task, so the paper must not claim it ran its own LLM inference.

**Figures.** All are full text width (5.5 in, single-column ICLR) and exported as PDF plus 300-DPI PNG:
- an overview schematic (the only `generate-concept-figure` use) near page 1–2;
- per-case interval score for the four reporters;
- per-case bias and coverage;
- an optional width-versus-N figure.

The supplement covers estimator details, per-case and per-seed tables, the search-stage variants, evaluation provenance and the LLM usage disclosure.

**References.** Most of `references.bib` is irrelevant (medical and similar entries). The writer should cite only the adaptive-data-analysis entries. The starter-literature works (MMLU-Pro, DSPy, MIPRO, Ladder and others) are not in the bib and need verified retrieval before citing.

I also appended the framing decision to `memory.md`, `global_memory/memory.md` and `global_memory/memory.jsonl`.
